{"parentUuid":"b6563e48-6bfb-459d-98db-fe5201d01ee1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acbe77fbda04756f7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FEAwZHDyNFuzduvE7BqmSd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xm4CjhJKLPMLP9iFn4bXcy","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"electromagnetism-like algorithm EM facility layout 2024 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7184,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":324,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7184},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7184,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyRbNMTv7hjeZ3DbQQ8","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"738170e1-e22b-4e91-be24-c73a4788958c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:27.515Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f7ed1c8f-41eb-42f3-b86d-48cf380b44db","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"acbe77fbda04756f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ML9TBq1DTU4XKgW3g9bHrf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gravitational Search Algorithm GSA packing placement 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EQGSA-DPW: A Quantum-GSA Algorithm-Based Data Placement for Scientific Workflow in Cloud Computing Environment | Journal of Grid Computing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10723-024-09771-5\"},{\"title\":\"A Manifold‐Guided Gravitational Search Algorithm for High‐Dimensional Global Optimization Problems - Su - 2024 - International Journal of Intelligent Systems - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1155/2024/5806437\"},{\"title\":\"A Multi-Layered Gravitational Search Algorithm for Function Optimization and Real-World Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.ieee-jas.net/article/doi/10.1109/JAS.2020.1003462\"},{\"title\":\"GSA: A Gravitational Search Algorithm - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0020025509001200\"},{\"title\":\"GSA: a Gravitational Search Algorithm | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222853813_GSA_a_Gravitational_Search_Algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"MAR-GSA: : Mixed attraction and repulsion based gravitational search algorithm: Information Sciences: an International Journal: Vol 662, No C\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1016/j.ins.2024.120250\"},{\"title\":\"Gravitational Search Algorithm (GSA) - File Exchange - MATLAB Central\",\"url\":\"https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/27756-gravitational-search-algorithm-gsa\"},{\"title\":\"Improved Gravitational Search Algorithm Based on Adaptive Strategies | MDPI\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/1099-4300/24/12/1826\"},{\"title\":\"Multi-strategy collaborative optimization of gravitational search algorithm | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-13215-9\"},{\"title\":\"A new Cumulative Gravitational Search algorithm for optimal placement of FACT device to minimize system loss in the deregulated electrical power environment | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/303320668_A_new_Cumulative_Gravitational_Search_algorithm_for_optimal_placement_of_FACT_device_to_minimize_system_loss_in_the_deregulated_electrical_power_environment\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Gravitational Search Algorithm (GSA) and its applications in packing and placement during 2024-2025:\n\n## Overview of GSA\n\nThe Gravitational Search Algorithm (GSA) is an optimization algorithm constructed based on the law of Gravity and the notion of mass interactions. GSA is a physics-based meta-heuristic algorithm inspired by Newton's law of universal gravitation.\n\n## Recent Applications and Improvements (2024-2025)\n\nSeveral notable developments in GSA research have emerged recently:\n\n1. **Quantum-Enhanced GSA for Data Placement**: EQGSA-DPW, a novel algorithm leveraging quantum computing and swarm intelligence optimization, aims to optimize data placement for scientific workflow by considering multiple objectives like transmission bandwidth, cost and energy consumption, and improves the GSA algorithm by using the log-sigmoid transfer function as a gravitational constant.\n\n2. **Manifold-Guided GSA**: A manifold-guided gravitational search algorithm (MGGSA) combines GSA with manifold learning to solve high-dimensional optimization problems.\n\n3. **Mixed Attraction and Repulsion GSA**: A fitness normalization with mass shift strategy creates a situation where gravity and repulsion are mixed, a global best mechanism with weights is incorporated into the velocity update formula, and an empirical formula for the initial gravitational constant related to the size of the solution space is proposed.\n\n4. **Multi-Strategy Collaborative Optimization**: To address shortcomings such as falling into local optima, slow convergence, and low solution accuracy, multi-strategy collaborative optimization approaches balance global exploration and local exploitation.\n\nThese developments demonstrate active research into improving GSA's effectiveness for various placement and optimization problems in 2024-2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"89051d52-c74a-4f75-90f9-1db32b86586a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:32.875Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f7ed1c8f-41eb-42f3-b86d-48cf380b44db","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ddfaccda-d24a-41bc-91fc-b3aa15cc506c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"acbe77fbda04756f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014AyjCJwWM3GhCyrecsWER9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"crystallization heuristic optimization rectangle packing 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Model-Based Heuristic for Packing Soft Rotated Rectangles in an Optimized Convex Container with Prohibited Zones\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/13/3/493\"},{\"title\":\"An efficient heuristic algorithm for two-dimensional rectangular packing problem with central rectangle\",\"url\":\"https://www.aimsciences.org/article/doi/10.3934/jimo.2018164\"},{\"title\":\"An efficient constructive heuristic for the rectangular packing problem with rotations | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0295206\"},{\"title\":\"Neural-Driven Constructive Heuristic for 2D Robotic Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/14/10/1956\"},{\"title\":\"An efficient heuristic algorithm for rectangle-packing problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220674353_An_efficient_heuristic_algorithm_for_rectangle-packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal rectangle packing\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/spr/annopr/v179y2010i1p261-29510.1007-s10479-008-0463-6.html\"},{\"title\":\"1 December 2025 Optimization of 3D-Printed Structured Packings –\",\"url\":\"https://chemrxiv.org/doi/pdf/10.26434/chemrxiv-2025-54lbn\"},{\"title\":\"Transformer-based placement heuristic for online 2D strip packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360835225006102\"},{\"title\":\"An efficient constructive heuristic for the rectangular packing problem with rotations - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10754432/\"},{\"title\":\"A new approach for bin packing problem using knowledge reuse and improved heuristic | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-81749-5\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about crystallization heuristic optimization and rectangle packing research in 2025:\n\n## Recent Rectangle Packing Research (2025)\n\nThe search results reveal several significant developments in rectangle packing optimization:\n\n### Latest Publications\n\nA recent model-based heuristic study for packing soft rotated rectangles was published in January 2025. The approach allows soft rectangles to be freely translated and rotated, with fixed areas and variable dimensions within certain limits.\n\nAnother 2025 study published in May proposes a novel neural-driven constructive heuristic that employs a population of simple feed-forward neural networks trained using black-box optimization via the Covariance Matrix Adaptation Evolution Strategy (CMA-ES).\n\n### Advanced Optimization Approaches\n\nRecent research shows a trend toward hybrid methods. One approach leverages a lightweight neural network trained via black-box optimization to dynamically evaluate item placement decisions. Additionally, the hybrid algorithm combining heuristic algorithm and meta-heuristic algorithm is currently the mainstream method for solving 2D irregular packing problems.\n\n### Algorithm Development\n\nMaxRects is described as the best-known heuristic family for the problem, with research continuing on various optimization techniques for placement and sequencing of rectangular items.\n\nHowever, I should note that the search results don't contain specific information about a \"crystallization heuristic\" specifically applied to rectangle packing in 2025. The results focus on other heuristic and optimization approaches for this problem domain.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"10bf0216-b356-41df-815f-5e07c29ed4b7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:33.019Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ddfaccda-d24a-41bc-91fc-b3aa15cc506c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"738170e1-e22b-4e91-be24-c73a4788958c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"acbe77fbda04756f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xm4CjhJKLPMLP9iFn4bXcy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"electromagnetism-like algorithm EM facility layout 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Electromagnetism-like Mechanism Algorithm | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-03404-1_21\"},{\"title\":\"Location and transportation planning in supply chains under uncertainty and congestion by using an improved electromagnetism-like algorithm | Journal of Intelligent Manufacturing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10845-015-1191-9\"},{\"title\":\"A revised electromagnetism-like mechanism for layout design of reconfigurable manufacturing system | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/257177459_A_revised_electromagnetism-like_mechanism_for_layout_design_of_reconfigurable_manufacturing_system\"},{\"title\":\"New Optimization Strategies for Synthesizing RF, Microwave, mmWave, and Optical Devices\",\"url\":\"https://ieeeaps.org/new-optimization-strategies-for-synthesizing-rf-microwave-mmwave-and-optical-devices\"},{\"title\":\"What are the EMC simulation software? | Shenzhen EUTTEST\",\"url\":\"https://www.euttest.com/en/resources/emc-simulation-software.html\"},{\"title\":\"Recent Advances in Computational Electromagnetics for Emerging Challenges and Applications\",\"url\":\"https://ieeeaps.org/recent-advances-in-computational-electromagnetics-for-emerging-challenges-and-applications\"},{\"title\":\"Improving the prediction of energy performance of building using electromagnetic field optimization algorithm | International Journal of Low-Carbon Technologies | Oxford Academic\",\"url\":\"https://academic.oup.com/ijlct/article/doi/10.1093/ijlct/ctae113/7715675\"},{\"title\":\"A guidance to intelligent metamaterials and metamaterials intelligence | Nature Communications\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-56122-3\"},{\"title\":\"A New Competitive Implementation of the Electromagnetism-Like Algorithm for Global Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-21407-8_36\"},{\"title\":\"Electromagnetic wave propagation algorithm: A novel electromagnetic wave propagation-inspired optimizer for engineering applications - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2090447925003569\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here are the key findings about the electromagnetism-like algorithm and facility layout:\n\n## Overview of the Electromagnetism-Like Algorithm\n\nThe electromagnetism-like mechanism (EM) algorithm is inspired by the theory of electromagnetism. It is a population-based stochastic global optimization algorithm that uses an attraction-repulsion mechanism to move sample points towards the optimal.\n\n## Application to Facility Layout\n\nThe EM algorithm has been applied to facility layout problems in manufacturing systems. A revised electromagnetism-like mechanism has been used for layout design of reconfigurable manufacturing systems. More specifically, the electromagnetism-like mechanism was adapted to solve the layout design problem in reconfigurable manufacturing systems, with the approach aiming to reduce costs, namely the system reconfiguration and the material handling costs.\n\nA hybrid electromagnetism-like algorithm has also been applied to solve the dynamic inter/intra cell layout problem.\n\n## Recent Developments (2024-2025)\n\nThe search results show that a hybrid meta-heuristic algorithm based on electromagnetism-like algorithm and simulated annealing concepts has been designed for solving supply chain and facility location problems. Additionally, a new physics-based meta-heuristic optimization technique called the Electromagnetic Wave Propagation Algorithm (EMWPA) has been introduced, which models the propagation behavior of electromagnetic waves for global search diversity.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7d6efedf-2ed2-43a0-abb8-38e16345ac9e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:33.264Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"738170e1-e22b-4e91-be24-c73a4788958c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b6563e48-6bfb-459d-98db-fe5201d01ee1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"acbe77fbda04756f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014CtNgpXpZdZWnwfj2CjeAy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"particle swarm optimization 2D packing layout 2025 benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Particle Swarm Optimization Algorithm for a 2-D Irregular Strip Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.scirp.org/journal/paperinformation?paperid=29233\"},{\"title\":\"A Particle Swarm Optimization Algorithm for a 2-D Irregular Strip Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://file.scirp.org/Html/2-1040217_29233.htm\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ElkmanY/pso: This repository contains the standard Particle Swarm Optimization code (Matlab M-file) for optimizing the benchmark function.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ElkmanY/pso\"},{\"title\":\"A Layout Pattern Based Particle Swarm Optimization for Constrained Packing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://scialert.net/fulltext/?doi=itj.2012.1722.1729\"},{\"title\":\"A new approach for bin packing problem using knowledge reuse and improved heuristic | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-81749-5\"},{\"title\":\"Sequence Transfer-Based Particle Swarm Optimization Algorithm for Irregular Packing Problems | IEEE Journals & Magazine | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9543656/\"},{\"title\":\"Fidelity-adaptive evolutionary optimization algorithm for 2D irregular cutting and packing problem | Journal of Intelligent Manufacturing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10845-024-02329-y\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - maramire/SP_PSO: A serial and parallel algorithm to solve regular 2D strip packing using Particle Swarm Optimization and a recursive heuristic.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/maramire/SP_PSO\"},{\"title\":\"Two-dimensional irregular packing problems: A review\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/mechanical-engineering/articles/10.3389/fmech.2022.966691/pdf\"},{\"title\":\"2-Dimensional rectangles-in-circles packing and stock cutting with particle swarm optimization | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/323000749_2-Dimensional_rectangles-in-circles_packing_and_stock_cutting_with_particle_swarm_optimization\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found several relevant sources about particle swarm optimization (PSO) applied to 2D packing layout problems:\n\n## Overview\n\nParticle swarm optimization algorithm is used as a sequence optimization algorithm for meta-heuristic approaches to solving 2D irregular packing problems, along with other evolutionary techniques.\n\n## Recent Research and Applications\n\nHybrid algorithms combining heuristic and meta-heuristic approaches are the mainstream method for solving 2D irregular packing problems.\n\nSeveral recent studies have advanced PSO methods for packing:\n\n- A sequence transfer-based particle swarm optimization algorithm (ST-PSO) was proposed to solve multi-constraint packing problems, with a piece-matching strategy based on an improved shape context algorithm and a piece-sequencing generation strategy for PSO initialization.\n\n- A Layout Pattern Based Particle Swarm Optimization algorithm (LPPSO) was presented for solving two-dimensional packing problems with constraints, where individuals are constructed according to non-isomorphic layout patterns.\n\n- A fidelity-adaptive evolutionary optimization (FAEO) method was proposed to speed up the optimization process by using different nesting strategies at appropriate optimization stages, with this work published in 2025.\n\n## Benchmarking\n\nResearchers have tested these algorithms on benchmark datasets. Results from SwarmNest (a PSO-based approach) for 31 benchmark data sets available in the literature were compared with published results, producing better solutions or at least equal solutions to the best known solutions for 10 out of the 31 benchmark data sets.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"194e2384-5607-474e-875e-7d71ed675fba","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:34.166Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b6563e48-6bfb-459d-98db-fe5201d01ee1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
